1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:08,091
["ABELYANA" BY MAKI PLAYING]

2
00:00:24,149 --> 00:00:25,150
<i>Enrico.</i>

3
00:00:27,861 --> 00:00:30,405
<i>It's way past your 10-day deadline</i>
<i>with Boss Zandro.</i>

4
00:00:30,488 --> 00:00:33,575
<i>I've sent Zandro 20,000 pesos.</i>

5
00:00:34,075 --> 00:00:36,828
<i>You owe him 20,000 dollars.</i>

6
00:00:36,911 --> 00:00:38,288
<i>Do you think I'm an idiot?</i>

7
00:00:38,371 --> 00:00:42,500
- [BOTH GRUNTING]
- [BLOWS LAND]

8
00:00:43,126 --> 00:00:44,544
[THUG GROANS]

9
00:00:44,627 --> 00:00:46,171
[PANTING]

10
00:00:54,888 --> 00:00:56,347
[PANICKED SHOUTS]

11
00:00:56,431 --> 00:00:57,557
<i>Help!</i>

12
00:00:57,640 --> 00:00:59,684
<i>Let's take him to the hospital!</i>

13
00:00:59,768 --> 00:01:02,937
<i>Okay. Will it be possible to do</i>
<i>in eight weeks?</i>

14
00:01:03,021 --> 00:01:04,105
<i>Six weeks.</i>

15
00:01:04,189 --> 00:01:06,232
<i>Very confident, Mr. Valentin.</i>

16
00:01:06,316 --> 00:01:07,692
<i>Then we have a deal.</i>

17
00:01:07,776 --> 00:01:09,027
<i>- Sir Andy, thank you.</i>
<i>- Yeah.</i>

18
00:01:09,110 --> 00:01:10,403
<i>Thank you. Thank you very much.</i>

19
00:01:10,487 --> 00:01:12,947
[BILLY] <i>Thank you. Thank you.</i>

20
00:01:13,031 --> 00:01:15,033
<i>Gosh, what would I do</i>

21
00:01:15,116 --> 00:01:17,911
<i>if I didn't have</i>
<i>my ridiculously cocky best friend?</i>

22
00:01:17,994 --> 00:01:22,123
<i>He's talented, handsome, and smells good!</i>

23
00:01:22,207 --> 00:01:23,583
<i>He's perfect!</i>

24
00:01:23,666 --> 00:01:25,668
<i>All he's missing is a girlfriend.</i>

25
00:01:25,752 --> 00:01:28,421
<i>We'll find one for him. Mm!</i>

26
00:01:31,841 --> 00:01:34,302
[NURSE]<i> May I speak</i>
<i>with Benilda Cariño?</i>

27
00:01:34,385 --> 00:01:35,345
[BILLY] <i>Who's this?</i>

28
00:01:35,428 --> 00:01:38,640
<i>Ma'am, this is Nurse Anj</i>
<i>from St. John Hospital.</i>

29
00:01:38,723 --> 00:01:40,809
<i>You're listed as an emergency contact.</i>

30
00:01:40,892 --> 00:01:42,977
<i>For patient Enrico Dominguez.</i>

31
00:01:44,979 --> 00:01:47,357
[MONITOR BEEPING]

32
00:01:49,025 --> 00:01:50,527
<i>What's your relationship to the patient?</i>

33
00:01:51,694 --> 00:01:54,781
[BILLY] <i>I can't believe he put me down</i>
<i>as his emergency contact.</i>

34
00:01:54,864 --> 00:01:56,282
<i>What was he expecting?</i>

35
00:01:56,366 --> 00:01:57,742
<i>You went to see him.</i>

36
00:01:57,826 --> 00:01:59,452
<i>You even paid his bill.</i>

37
00:01:59,536 --> 00:02:02,580
<i>Of course I had to pay for it. Otherwise,</i>
<i>the hospital might come after me later.</i>

38
00:02:02,664 --> 00:02:04,457
[MAN] <i>So you're Enrico's daughter.</i>

39
00:02:04,541 --> 00:02:07,919
<i>Your father owes my boss</i>
<i>a huge sum of money.</i>

40
00:02:08,002 --> 00:02:09,045
<i>Over a million pesos.</i>

41
00:02:09,129 --> 00:02:12,048
<i>It's his debt, not mine.</i>

42
00:02:12,132 --> 00:02:13,675
<i>He doesn't have the money to pay it back.</i>

43
00:02:14,259 --> 00:02:16,386
<i>Then he shouldn't have borrowed</i>
<i>the money in the first place.</i>

44
00:02:16,970 --> 00:02:20,265
<i>And your boss</i>
<i>shouldn't have lent it to him.</i>

45
00:02:20,348 --> 00:02:21,432
<i>Wait a minute.</i>

46
00:02:21,516 --> 00:02:22,976
<i>- Hey!</i>
<i>- Jordan!</i>

47
00:02:23,059 --> 00:02:24,394
<i>- That's your problem!</i>
<i>- Jordan!</i>

48
00:02:24,477 --> 00:02:26,646
<i>My friend has nothing to do with it, okay?</i>

49
00:02:26,729 --> 00:02:27,897
<i>- Come on, let's just go.</i>
<i>- Okay?!</i>

50
00:02:27,981 --> 00:02:29,149
<i>- That's enough! Jordan!</i>
<i>- Let go!</i>

51
00:02:41,244 --> 00:02:45,290
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

52
00:02:45,373 --> 00:02:47,292
- [SIGHS] No…
- [PHONE RINGING]

53
00:02:48,001 --> 00:02:51,588
[PHONE RINGING]

54
00:02:53,464 --> 00:02:54,299
Hello?

55
00:02:54,382 --> 00:02:55,383
Hey.

56
00:02:56,259 --> 00:02:58,636
I just called to check if you're okay.

57
00:02:59,470 --> 00:03:00,680
I'm okay.

58
00:03:00,763 --> 00:03:02,307
Don't worry about me.

59
00:03:02,390 --> 00:03:03,516
How could I not?

60
00:03:04,058 --> 00:03:05,476
Look.

61
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:07,020
I just thought you should know.

62
00:03:07,979 --> 00:03:09,355
I'm at the police station.

63
00:03:09,439 --> 00:03:11,566
What? What are you doing there?

64
00:03:11,649 --> 00:03:14,068
I don't want to add to your problems,

65
00:03:14,152 --> 00:03:17,614
but I'm sure sooner or later,
you'll find out anyway.

66
00:03:18,740 --> 00:03:19,866
[JORDAN] <i>I just found out</i>

67
00:03:20,742 --> 00:03:22,410
Bea got off the hook again.

68
00:03:22,994 --> 00:03:25,830
Caloy denies that they were accomplices.

69
00:03:25,914 --> 00:03:27,040
What?

70
00:03:28,207 --> 00:03:29,208
How did that happen?

71
00:03:29,292 --> 00:03:32,337
Of course, Caloy would deny it.

72
00:03:32,420 --> 00:03:35,256
Aren't there other ways to check?
What about Caloy's phone?

73
00:03:35,340 --> 00:03:36,966
They didn't find a phone on Caloy.

74
00:03:37,842 --> 00:03:39,177
He probably discarded it.

75
00:03:39,260 --> 00:03:40,303
With Bea…

76
00:03:40,845 --> 00:03:41,763
I'm sorry, dude.

77
00:03:41,846 --> 00:03:43,264
[JORDAN] <i>They didn't find anything.</i>

78
00:03:43,348 --> 00:03:44,766
<i>They're meticulous.</i>

79
00:03:45,892 --> 00:03:47,435
So, I came.

80
00:03:47,518 --> 00:03:48,937
I had to try and do something.

81
00:03:52,148 --> 00:03:55,109
Jordan, don't put yourself
in danger again, okay?

82
00:03:55,193 --> 00:03:56,945
No. I promise.

83
00:03:57,028 --> 00:03:57,904
I'll be safe.

84
00:03:59,030 --> 00:04:00,073
Anyway, that's it.

85
00:04:01,157 --> 00:04:02,784
I didn't want to stress you out. Okay?

86
00:04:02,867 --> 00:04:04,035
So relax.

87
00:04:05,662 --> 00:04:06,746
Okay.

88
00:04:07,664 --> 00:04:08,498
Thank you.

89
00:04:08,581 --> 00:04:10,458
Please, be careful over there, okay?

90
00:04:10,541 --> 00:04:11,918
I'll keep you posted.

91
00:04:12,877 --> 00:04:19,884
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

92
00:04:25,598 --> 00:04:26,766
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

93
00:04:44,367 --> 00:04:51,082
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

94
00:05:41,049 --> 00:05:42,258
[JORDAN] Okay.

95
00:05:43,092 --> 00:05:44,761
Cooperate with us.

96
00:05:45,553 --> 00:05:48,806
Then we could consider

97
00:05:48,890 --> 00:05:50,475
dropping your other cases.

98
00:05:52,143 --> 00:05:53,936
I won't fall for your trap.

99
00:05:56,606 --> 00:05:58,357
But you already have, haven't you?

100
00:06:02,612 --> 00:06:03,821
Caloy.

101
00:06:04,530 --> 00:06:06,115
Bea abandoned you.

102
00:06:06,949 --> 00:06:09,744
Why are you still protecting her?

103
00:06:09,827 --> 00:06:14,248
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

104
00:06:14,332 --> 00:06:15,541
What are you talking about?

105
00:06:15,625 --> 00:06:18,336
Bea has nothing to do with this.

106
00:06:18,419 --> 00:06:20,546
I did it on my own.

107
00:06:22,882 --> 00:06:24,092
Because I love her.

108
00:06:24,967 --> 00:06:26,427
You planned this.

109
00:06:28,262 --> 00:06:29,847
But why did you target Billy?

110
00:06:30,473 --> 00:06:31,682
Hmm?

111
00:06:32,350 --> 00:06:33,267
Why?!

112
00:06:34,644 --> 00:06:36,938
I don't know.

113
00:06:37,021 --> 00:06:42,652
[TENSE MUSIC FADING]

114
00:06:49,117 --> 00:06:51,327
Oh, it's already late.

115
00:06:52,245 --> 00:06:53,538
[BEA] Uh…

116
00:06:53,621 --> 00:06:54,497
Ma!

117
00:06:54,580 --> 00:06:56,332
I'm a supervisor,

118
00:06:56,415 --> 00:06:58,960
so I can clock in at any time.

119
00:07:00,128 --> 00:07:01,045
Oh.

120
00:07:01,129 --> 00:07:02,255
Sorry, dear.

121
00:07:02,839 --> 00:07:05,424
The landlord came earlier.

122
00:07:05,508 --> 00:07:07,176
She was asking for the rent.

123
00:07:07,260 --> 00:07:09,178
I told her,

124
00:07:09,262 --> 00:07:12,807
"Don't be impatient!
My daughter will pay you."

125
00:07:12,890 --> 00:07:15,476
"She might even slap you with her money!"

126
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:17,645
[CHUCKLES] That's right, Ma.

127
00:07:17,728 --> 00:07:19,188
[BEA] I won't just slap her with it.

128
00:07:19,272 --> 00:07:21,482
I'll choke her with my money.

129
00:07:21,566 --> 00:07:23,734
[MARIELA CHUCKLES]

130
00:07:23,818 --> 00:07:25,528
Okay, I'll get going then.

131
00:07:25,611 --> 00:07:26,863
All right.

132
00:07:26,946 --> 00:07:33,953
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

133
00:07:39,167 --> 00:07:40,001
[BILLY] Auntie Pres.

134
00:07:40,084 --> 00:07:42,336
Oh, Billy! I'm sorry.

135
00:07:42,420 --> 00:07:44,172
- I forgot to call you.
- It's okay.

136
00:07:44,255 --> 00:07:46,924
They said Sir Eric couldn't
come in to work today.

137
00:07:47,842 --> 00:07:49,719
Huh? It's okay.

138
00:07:49,802 --> 00:07:52,346
But it's a shame
this will be wasted, Auntie Pres.

139
00:07:55,933 --> 00:07:57,268
Billy, are you all right?

140
00:08:01,522 --> 00:08:03,941
I went to the hospital earlier,
Auntie Pres.

141
00:08:04,025 --> 00:08:07,737
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

142
00:08:07,820 --> 00:08:09,030
Why?

143
00:08:17,079 --> 00:08:18,789
Thank you.

144
00:08:19,957 --> 00:08:26,964
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

145
00:08:28,758 --> 00:08:30,051
Who paid for it?

146
00:08:30,134 --> 00:08:31,761
Your daughter did.

147
00:08:33,137 --> 00:08:35,348
- She came here?
- Mm.

148
00:08:35,431 --> 00:08:37,850
You were asleep when she visited you.

149
00:08:42,230 --> 00:08:44,482
Did she know about this?

150
00:08:44,565 --> 00:08:46,192
No, sir.

151
00:08:47,735 --> 00:08:48,861
Thank you.

152
00:08:48,945 --> 00:08:55,284
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

153
00:08:56,827 --> 00:08:59,747
[BILLY] <i>The bill has been paid,</i>
<i>but please,</i>

154
00:08:59,830 --> 00:09:02,500
<i>don't make me your emergency contact</i>

155
00:09:02,583 --> 00:09:06,462
<i>because next time, I won't be coming.</i>

156
00:09:06,546 --> 00:09:12,802
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

157
00:09:12,885 --> 00:09:15,263
Your father really is the worst.

158
00:09:15,346 --> 00:09:17,223
He even got you involved in his debts.

159
00:09:19,183 --> 00:09:21,060
I'm not surprised anymore, Auntie Pres.

160
00:09:23,312 --> 00:09:26,482
When I found out that he became
a scammer in Canada,

161
00:09:27,692 --> 00:09:30,653
I already knew that
he was only after money.

162
00:09:30,736 --> 00:09:33,948
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

163
00:09:34,031 --> 00:09:35,575
Can you still handle it?

164
00:09:35,658 --> 00:09:37,368
Of course.

165
00:09:39,954 --> 00:09:41,664
What if he comes back?

166
00:09:41,747 --> 00:09:46,544
Especially when he finds out that
you paid for his hospital bill,

167
00:09:46,627 --> 00:09:50,339
he might get the wrong idea
and think that you care about him.

168
00:09:50,423 --> 00:09:52,717
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

169
00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:55,511
It's the first and last time
that I'll help him, Auntie Pres.

170
00:09:56,971 --> 00:09:58,431
Let's just leave it at that.

171
00:09:59,265 --> 00:10:01,350
There are more important things

172
00:10:01,434 --> 00:10:03,853
that I need to take care of
before that man.

173
00:10:03,936 --> 00:10:10,151
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

174
00:10:16,240 --> 00:10:18,242
Why can't I go upstairs?!

175
00:10:18,326 --> 00:10:21,746
We really can't let you, ma'am.
We were told not to let you go upstairs.

176
00:10:21,829 --> 00:10:22,872
Who said that?

177
00:10:22,955 --> 00:10:25,499
Miss, I didn't do anything wrong!
Why can't I--

178
00:10:25,583 --> 00:10:27,543
[HEELS CLACKING]

179
00:10:27,627 --> 00:10:29,712
Ms. Talia! Ms. Talia!

180
00:10:29,795 --> 00:10:32,173
What are you doing here?
I thought you were in jail!

181
00:10:32,256 --> 00:10:34,967
What? I've done nothing wrong!

182
00:10:35,051 --> 00:10:36,886
You were working together with that thief!

183
00:10:36,969 --> 00:10:38,554
No! That's not true!

184
00:10:38,638 --> 00:10:40,431
- Whoever said that--
- Security, take her outside!

185
00:10:40,514 --> 00:10:42,058
- Ms. Talia, I just need a job!
- Now, go!

186
00:10:42,141 --> 00:10:44,310
- I'm begging you, Ms. Talia! Please!
- Please leave, ma'am.

187
00:10:44,393 --> 00:10:45,811
- Ms. Talia!
- Billy?

188
00:10:45,895 --> 00:10:48,689
Bea's here and she's making a scene.

189
00:10:48,773 --> 00:10:52,401
I thought our plan would put her in jail.

190
00:10:53,527 --> 00:10:55,571
Unfortunately, Ms. Talia,

191
00:10:55,655 --> 00:10:59,158
we still don't have substantial evidence
linking her to the robbery.

192
00:10:59,241 --> 00:11:01,160
Her claims to the police
are still consistent

193
00:11:01,243 --> 00:11:03,537
that Carlos Toledo was harassing her.

194
00:11:03,621 --> 00:11:05,331
We planned this!

195
00:11:05,414 --> 00:11:07,083
What are we going to do now?

196
00:11:07,708 --> 00:11:10,503
Don't worry, Ms. Talia,
you've helped enough.

197
00:11:10,586 --> 00:11:11,796
Leave it to me now.

198
00:11:11,879 --> 00:11:13,047
Okay, Billy.

199
00:11:13,130 --> 00:11:16,175
Whatever you need, just tell me.

200
00:11:16,258 --> 00:11:19,345
Okay. Thank you so much, Ms. Talia.

201
00:11:19,428 --> 00:11:25,810
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

202
00:11:28,354 --> 00:11:29,313
Marj!

203
00:11:29,397 --> 00:11:30,398
[MARJ] Hm?

204
00:11:31,524 --> 00:11:32,441
Hey.

205
00:11:32,525 --> 00:11:33,818
We need to talk.

206
00:11:34,819 --> 00:11:36,320
It's about your vlog.

207
00:11:36,821 --> 00:11:37,988
[MARJ] What's wrong with it?

208
00:11:39,115 --> 00:11:40,574
[VALERIE] It's missing something!

209
00:11:40,658 --> 00:11:43,577
You should've also mentioned
his partner-in-crime, Bea Mercado.

210
00:11:44,245 --> 00:11:46,247
<i>- Stop resisting!</i>
- [CALOY] <i>Hold on.</i>

211
00:11:46,789 --> 00:11:49,417
- [OFFICER] <i>Get in!</i>
- [CALOY GRUNTING] <i>Sir…</i>

212
00:11:49,500 --> 00:11:51,043
- [SIGHS]
- [OFFICER] <i>Let's go!</i>

213
00:11:51,127 --> 00:11:56,298
<i>Justice said "not today"</i>
<i>and karma handled it.</i>

214
00:11:56,382 --> 00:11:57,550
[POLICE SIREN WAILING]

215
00:11:59,135 --> 00:12:00,886
You're right!

216
00:12:00,970 --> 00:12:05,474
You know, I can't believe that
she was released again.

217
00:12:05,558 --> 00:12:07,059
[VALERIE] It's fine.

218
00:12:07,143 --> 00:12:08,853
Let's just make another vlog about it.

219
00:12:08,936 --> 00:12:10,521
Okay. Let's do it.

220
00:12:10,604 --> 00:12:13,941
And we'll let the world know
that she's also a criminal.

221
00:12:14,024 --> 00:12:15,067
Yeah.

222
00:12:15,151 --> 00:12:17,987
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

223
00:12:18,070 --> 00:12:21,157
<i>Did Jordan really think…</i>
[CHUCKLES]

224
00:12:21,240 --> 00:12:22,658
…he could outsmart me of all people?

225
00:12:22,741 --> 00:12:26,245
<i>Ah, it hurts.</i>

226
00:12:26,328 --> 00:12:27,997
<i>That's because you weren't careful.</i>

227
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:29,665
<i>For heaven's sake, Caloy!</i>

228
00:12:29,748 --> 00:12:31,041
<i>What is wrong with you?!</i>

229
00:12:31,125 --> 00:12:34,336
<i>Every single one of your plans fails!</i>
<i>You messed up again!</i>

230
00:12:34,420 --> 00:12:40,718
[FOREBODING MUSIC CONTINUES]

231
00:12:44,430 --> 00:12:46,474
What are you doing here?

232
00:12:49,560 --> 00:12:52,021
Can you please talk to your people?

233
00:12:52,104 --> 00:12:53,981
Let the world know that I'm a criminal?!

234
00:12:54,064 --> 00:12:57,193
Maybe they want to know
what a real criminal is.

235
00:12:57,776 --> 00:12:58,861
Why?

236
00:12:58,944 --> 00:13:00,738
Aren't you one?

237
00:13:01,322 --> 00:13:02,281
So true.

238
00:13:05,993 --> 00:13:09,163
Even our own house isn't safe
from your anger.

239
00:13:10,164 --> 00:13:12,082
Neither is my family.

240
00:13:12,166 --> 00:13:14,376
Do you think you're going to scare me?

241
00:13:14,460 --> 00:13:17,004
Enjoy your freedom
because it won't last long.

242
00:13:19,590 --> 00:13:21,050
Oh! And by the way…

243
00:13:23,511 --> 00:13:26,013
Orange looks good on you.

244
00:13:26,096 --> 00:13:32,102
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

245
00:13:46,784 --> 00:13:52,957
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

246
00:13:57,628 --> 00:13:58,754
[SNIFFLES]

247
00:14:00,798 --> 00:14:01,882
[SNIFFLES]

248
00:14:15,896 --> 00:14:21,652
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

249
00:14:24,822 --> 00:14:29,869
[MUSIC BECOMES STIRRING]

250
00:14:31,996 --> 00:14:33,122
[PHONE CHIMES]

251
00:14:48,137 --> 00:14:53,851
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

252
00:14:57,771 --> 00:15:01,901
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

253
00:15:09,992 --> 00:15:12,036
[PHONE RINGING]

254
00:15:13,037 --> 00:15:13,913
Ma!

255
00:15:15,164 --> 00:15:16,373
Uh,

256
00:15:16,457 --> 00:15:18,125
do you want to eat out?

257
00:15:19,126 --> 00:15:20,669
So we've sealed a partnership

258
00:15:20,753 --> 00:15:23,672
with Cipher Axis Security System.

259
00:15:23,756 --> 00:15:25,799
They will officially provide us

260
00:15:25,883 --> 00:15:28,010
- our cybersecurity.
- [MARJ] Ooh!

261
00:15:28,093 --> 00:15:31,722
And given that,
I asked them to be one of our partners

262
00:15:31,805 --> 00:15:33,641
for our Happily Ever After events.

263
00:15:33,724 --> 00:15:34,808
They said yes.

264
00:15:34,892 --> 00:15:39,146
And they assured us that
their system is secure.

265
00:15:39,229 --> 00:15:40,814
So congrats, team!

266
00:15:40,898 --> 00:15:42,608
- Yay!
- Yay!

267
00:15:42,691 --> 00:15:45,736
You did this while you were planning
what to do with Caloy?

268
00:15:47,237 --> 00:15:50,366
[VAL] As if Bea wasn't harassing
us just now.

269
00:15:50,449 --> 00:15:51,408
[SHUSHING]

270
00:15:51,492 --> 00:15:53,369
- It's okay. We won anyway.
- [PHONE CHIMES]

271
00:15:55,704 --> 00:15:57,164
WHAT HAPPENED WITH THESE GUYS?

272
00:15:57,247 --> 00:15:59,124
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

273
00:15:59,208 --> 00:16:00,292
Charm, what's wrong?

274
00:16:01,043 --> 00:16:02,378
[BREATHES DEEPLY]

275
00:16:02,461 --> 00:16:04,129
Ralph's mom sent this.

276
00:16:04,213 --> 00:16:05,798
[CHARM BREATHES DEEPLY]

277
00:16:05,881 --> 00:16:07,466
They saw it.

278
00:16:07,549 --> 00:16:09,009
And now, they're questioning me

279
00:16:09,093 --> 00:16:12,304
if they did the right thing
when they invested in us.

280
00:16:14,765 --> 00:16:16,392
But what's worse is,

281
00:16:16,976 --> 00:16:19,895
they're questioning
my relationship with Ralph.

282
00:16:19,979 --> 00:16:22,189
[SOBS] They said

283
00:16:22,940 --> 00:16:25,401
that we're involved with criminals.

284
00:16:26,276 --> 00:16:27,736
That we're a part of them.

285
00:16:27,820 --> 00:16:30,406
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

286
00:16:30,489 --> 00:16:32,700
Billy, sorry. I'm sorry.

287
00:16:32,783 --> 00:16:34,118
Just what am I doing?

288
00:16:34,201 --> 00:16:36,495
This is nothing compared
to what you're going through.

289
00:16:36,578 --> 00:16:38,706
- I'm sorry.
- Charm, don't be like that.

290
00:16:38,789 --> 00:16:42,835
There are no big or small problems
between friends, okay?

291
00:16:43,502 --> 00:16:44,753
- [SNIFFLES]
- Just let it all out.

292
00:16:44,837 --> 00:16:48,716
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

293
00:16:48,799 --> 00:16:49,967
It's okay.

294
00:16:52,469 --> 00:16:53,554
[SNIFFLES]

295
00:16:53,637 --> 00:16:55,264
[TONI] It's okay.

296
00:16:55,347 --> 00:16:56,682
[CHARM SOBS]

297
00:16:58,976 --> 00:17:01,478
[SNIFFLING, EXHALES HEAVILY]

298
00:17:02,104 --> 00:17:03,689
- [BILLY] Whoo-hoo!
- [CHARM] Group hug!

299
00:17:03,772 --> 00:17:05,482
[LAUGHING]

300
00:17:05,566 --> 00:17:07,901
Just ignore those posts, okay?

301
00:17:07,985 --> 00:17:09,028
[SNIFFLES]

302
00:17:13,449 --> 00:17:16,285
I'm still looking for a way
to trace Bea's father.

303
00:17:16,368 --> 00:17:19,621
I tried getting a copy
of her birth certificate,

304
00:17:19,705 --> 00:17:22,291
but it'll need an SPA or a court order.

305
00:17:22,374 --> 00:17:24,501
When I went to see Caloy,

306
00:17:24,585 --> 00:17:26,879
he still denies that Bea is involved.

307
00:17:26,962 --> 00:17:29,965
For an entrapment where both of them
should've been locked up.

308
00:17:30,049 --> 00:17:31,425
[JORDAN EXHALES HEAVILY]

309
00:17:31,508 --> 00:17:34,428
I tried to ask
what the real reason is for all this.

310
00:17:36,346 --> 00:17:37,473
If it's just for money.

311
00:17:37,556 --> 00:17:38,849
It's not about money.

312
00:17:38,932 --> 00:17:42,144
If it were, they would've asked
for some a long time ago.

313
00:17:42,644 --> 00:17:45,189
What? They're just like my father?

314
00:17:45,272 --> 00:17:48,025
They think I'm an ATM machine?

315
00:17:52,780 --> 00:17:54,031
Hold on.

316
00:17:54,114 --> 00:17:55,449
I'll just withdraw some money.

317
00:17:56,408 --> 00:17:59,411
[IMITATING ATM BEEPING SOUNDS]

318
00:17:59,495 --> 00:18:00,871
[JORDAN] Oops. I have zero balance.

319
00:18:00,954 --> 00:18:02,081
I don't get it!

320
00:18:02,164 --> 00:18:04,625
How do so many girls fall
for your lame jokes!

321
00:18:04,708 --> 00:18:05,876
- What the hell?
- [THUDS]

322
00:18:05,959 --> 00:18:12,925
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

323
00:18:20,224 --> 00:18:21,433
[WHISPERING] Is she okay?

324
00:18:29,274 --> 00:18:31,276
I thought you couldn't get to work today.

325
00:18:31,360 --> 00:18:32,820
Is everything okay?

326
00:18:33,695 --> 00:18:35,781
I got to fix my family emergency.

327
00:18:35,864 --> 00:18:36,740
[PRECIOUS] Mmm.

328
00:18:36,824 --> 00:18:38,575
I got to talk to my kids.

329
00:18:39,118 --> 00:18:40,536
It's okay now.

330
00:18:40,619 --> 00:18:41,912
Oh. That's good.

331
00:18:41,995 --> 00:18:45,833
Oh, by the way,
Billy wanted to give this to you.

332
00:18:45,916 --> 00:18:48,877
She was here earlier.
You just missed each other.

333
00:18:49,586 --> 00:18:51,004
She said thanks for everything.

334
00:18:51,630 --> 00:18:53,215
[PRECIOUS] And it's diabetic-friendly.

335
00:18:53,298 --> 00:18:54,424
Billy knows.

336
00:18:56,093 --> 00:18:57,386
Thanks.

337
00:18:57,469 --> 00:18:59,596
- She really didn't have to.
- [PRECIOUS TSKS]

338
00:18:59,680 --> 00:19:01,932
Well, she said it's
to thank you for everything.

339
00:19:02,015 --> 00:19:06,395
Actually, she's already been here twice,
but you just keep missing each other.

340
00:19:06,478 --> 00:19:08,272
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

341
00:19:08,355 --> 00:19:09,565
Yeah, it's a shame.

342
00:19:10,274 --> 00:19:12,359
Don't worry. There's always next time.

343
00:19:20,242 --> 00:19:25,455
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING, FADES]

344
00:19:26,331 --> 00:19:29,710
<i>I can't believe his mom</i>
<i>is still that controlling.</i>

345
00:19:29,793 --> 00:19:32,254
<i>Well, I'd rather have a controlling parent</i>
<i>than one who doesn't care.</i>

346
00:19:32,337 --> 00:19:35,549
<i>Not everyone has a parent</i>
<i>who worries about them.</i>

347
00:19:35,632 --> 00:19:36,758
<i>You have a point.</i>

348
00:19:36,842 --> 00:19:39,011
<i>I should be the one</i>
<i>handling this, Ma!</i>

349
00:19:39,595 --> 00:19:42,431
<i>It was Benilda Cariño herself</i>
<i>who invited me out for dinner.</i>

350
00:19:42,514 --> 00:19:45,517
<i>Ma, the legal issues</i>
<i>are not directly connected to LoveList.</i>

351
00:19:45,601 --> 00:19:49,688
<i>Now, I just want to know if the CEO</i>
<i>of LoveList is a decent woman.</i>

352
00:19:52,232 --> 00:19:54,026
[MARIELA] <i>That Billy thinks</i>

353
00:19:54,610 --> 00:19:56,361
<i>that she can just treat you</i>
<i>like you're nothing.</i>

354
00:19:56,445 --> 00:19:59,781
<i>That's why I told you</i>
<i>to just trust me, Ma.</i>

355
00:20:01,491 --> 00:20:04,119
<i>I have a reservation under Billy Cariño.</i>

356
00:20:04,203 --> 00:20:06,663
[MARIELA] <i>Are you following</i>
<i>my daughter?!</i>

357
00:20:08,665 --> 00:20:09,583
<i>Cat got your tongue?</i>

358
00:20:09,666 --> 00:20:11,501
<i>I'm not following your daughter.</i>

359
00:20:11,585 --> 00:20:12,669
<i>How dare you?!</i>

360
00:20:15,297 --> 00:20:17,799
<i>Like I told you before,</i>

361
00:20:17,883 --> 00:20:20,552
<i>it's your daughter</i>
<i>you need to talk to.</i>

362
00:20:23,096 --> 00:20:24,389
<i>Let go of my mother.</i>
